// __has_trivial_destructor over the madc carrier: a `var` is destroyed
// (madarray_destruct), so neither it nor a struct holding one is trivially
// destructible -- the CIR builder destroys both (class_needs_dtor). Oracle:
// g++ and clang++ with std::string in the carrier's place print
// "false true false".
struct S { var v; };
struct P { int a; };
println("{} {} {}", __has_trivial_destructor(S), __has_trivial_destructor(P),
        __has_trivial_destructor(var));
